      "notes": "Explain that particles are tiny pieces of matter represented by circles. In solids, particles cannot move past one another, so the shape stays fixed. Liquid particles move past one another, allowing the shape to change. Gas particles move freely and spread out. Solids and liquids are difficult to compress because their particles are already close together; gases have large gaps that can be reduced. Particles themselves do not shrink when a gas is compressed."
